{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Generate Closure Docs",
  "description": "Synthesizes AI-DLC workflow artifacts (aidlc-docs/) and implemented code into formal CIC project closure documentation (docs/). Run after implementation and deployment are complete.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "The user wants to generate project closure documentation. Delegate to the cic-documentation subagent with the following prompt:\n\n'Generate all CIC project closure documentation by synthesizing AI-DLC artifacts and implemented code.\n\n## Sources to Read\n\n1. **AI-DLC artifacts** — Read all files in aidlc-docs/ (requirements, designs, audit trail, state)\n2. **Implemented code** — Scan backend/lib/, backend/lambda/, frontend/app/ for actual implementation\n3. **Existing closure doc templates** — Read all files in docs/ to understand placeholder structure\n4. **Deployment outputs** — Check for CfnOutputs, deploy scripts, or deployment notes\n\n## Documents to Generate\n\nUpdate each closure doc in order. For each, replace [INSERT_*] placeholders with real content:\n\n1. **docs/architectureDeepDive.md** — Architecture diagram, service inventory, data flow, technology decisions, security boundaries. Primary sources: aidlc-docs/inception/application-design/, aidlc-docs/construction/*/infrastructure-design/, aidlc-docs/construction/*/nfr-requirements/tech-stack-decisions.md\n\n2. **docs/APIDoc.md** — All API endpoints with methods, paths, parameters, request/response examples, auth requirements. Primary sources: aidlc-docs/construction/*/functional-design/, actual Lambda handler code\n\n3. **docs/deploymentGuide.md** — Prerequisites, step-by-step deployment instructions, environment configuration, troubleshooting. Primary sources: aidlc-docs/construction/build-and-test/build-instructions.md, deploy.sh if it exists, CDK stack configuration\n\n4. **docs/userGuide.md** — End-user instructions for using the application. Primary sources: aidlc-docs/inception/user-stories/, aidlc-docs/inception/requirements/, frontend code inspection\n\n5. **docs/modificationGuide.md** — Developer guide for extending the project: project structure, component relationships, how to add features, coding conventions. Primary sources: aidlc-docs/inception/application-design/components.md, aidlc-docs/inception/application-design/component-dependency.md, code structure\n\n6. **docs/projectClosure.md** — Formal closure document: project summary, team, outcomes, lessons learned. Primary sources: aidlc-docs/audit.md, aidlc-docs/aidlc-state.md, all design artifacts\n\n7. **README.md** — Project overview, quick start, architecture summary, links to detailed docs. Synthesize from all of the above at summary level.\n\n## Quality Standards\n\n- Human-readable and streamlined — these are for stakeholders, not agents\n- Comprehensive but not verbose — cover everything important, skip implementation minutiae\n- Consistent cross-references — architecture doc matches API doc matches deployment guide\n- No [INSERT_*] placeholders remaining after generation\n- No AI-DLC jargon (aidlc-docs, units of work, stages) — translate to standard software terms\n\nAfter completing all documents, report which files were updated and highlight any gaps where information was unavailable.'"
  }
}
